# tally 2.2.1 P53 (R20, L §6.1): a member's warning lifted to the run's level names the member's
# things by the joint model's names where the instance has two keys too (review g4fix inv). Before W14:
# put[a, 2026-03] and the rows unprefixed.
=== top.tally
model fam
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30
  use a = "a/m.tally" sha256 "1e3b3d574324014553915e7a801e2c2f3ecc141d33199cabb5c1f4e99c009637"
=== a/m.tally
model mm
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input dn: int
input amt: money PLN
move put[k in ks, m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dn)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  dn = 5 "s"
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
version st1
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-10
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-05, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 10.00 PLN, fulfils: put[a, 2026-03]) "r1"
version st2
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-12
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-03-06, kind: transfers, leg cash from world to konto amount 12.00 PLN, fulfils: put[a, 2026-03]) "r2"
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect a.q
a.q: 50.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: put[a, 2026-01]
  unfulfilled: put[a, 2026-02]
  unfulfilled: put[b, 2026-01]
  unfulfilled: put[b, 2026-02]
  open: put[b, 2026-03]
  cut 2026-04-30
warning: WARN-LEGS the two observations of a.put[a, 2026-03] disagree: a.bank[r1] (10.00 PLN) and a.bank[r2] (12.00 PLN)
